# Line endings are LF in the tree and in the index, on every machine.
#
# The prod cleanup of 2026-09-04 was authored on the PC and committed CRLF into
# 156 files under src/, Test/ and harness/. That broke 11 of the 24 frozen
# SHA-256 pins in scripts/generate-schema-structural-assurance.sh, which are
# taken over raw file bytes: a line-ending flip is indistinguishable from an
# edit to a frozen source. This file makes the flip impossible rather than
# re-pinning after each one.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Two trees are byte-compared rather than read as text, so git must never
# rewrite them:
#
#   vendor/  is pinned against the upstream release by SHA-256
#            (scripts/generate-effect-runtime-census.sh, 150 pins;
#            scripts/check-schema-census.sh and check-schema-fields.sh).
#   generated/  holds the assurance and census goldens, compared byte for byte.
vendor/** -text
generated/** -text
